1	//! `goodfetch-collie-client` (ADR 0095): the Collie client crate, with no engine. It holds the
2	//! hand-written runtime, Collie's catalog types and every value a Collie connection hands out: Runs,
3	//! Sessions, Pages, Locators, results, errors and settings. Programs depend on their Product's
4	//! crate, `goodfetch-collie` or `goodfetch-foxhound`, which re-exports this one; only a library
5	//! meant to serve both Products depends on it, with a semver range.
6	//!
7	//! SDK API sketch: signatures only, no implementation. Function bodies are `unimplemented!()`, the
8	//! sketch's one departure from `STYLE.md`. In the SDK, the catalog's types come from
9	//! `goodfetch-protocol` (ADRs 0038, 0099); the sketch defines them here.
